Unicorn 2.1.4 with QEMU's interpreter (TCI) instead of generated code, so it
runs guest code without JIT. Applied after ipatool's unicorn-ios.patch.
GPLv2, like Unicorn (see README.md).

- qemu/tcg/tci.c and qemu/tcg/tci/: QEMU v5.0.0's interpreter
  (GPL-2.0-or-later), as Naville/unicorn ports it to Unicorn 2
  (https://github.com/Naville/unicorn, commits 795ba9a..53471ef, GPLv2),
  with its CMake option UNICORN_INTERPRETER and configure switch.
- Added here: GETPC() is the interpreter's place in the bytecode, per
  thread, as in QEMU 5 (exec-all.h), so faults inside helpers find their
  translation block; no MAP_JIT, and ipatool's write-protect toggle does
  nothing, since the code buffer is only ever read; configure defaults to
  no interpreter; uc_interpreter(), so WarpSign can tell this build apart.

